{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080722-shophouse-contract","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"timber-framed market shophouse (half-timber over limewashed stalls)","rationale":"Second pass, judged from the street. KEPT: dark_oak_log posts at x0/4/8/11 on the stall-wall columns, the stripped-spruce bressummer at y5 with lit redstone lamps over each stall (the shop sign), glazed bays A/B/C at y7-8, and the stripped-spruce wall plate at y9. FIXED 1 (roof was the weakest read, a ragged stack of mismatched courses): rebuilt it as one clean symmetric half-pitch roof. Its ridge is at z5, y13. The courses alternate bottom stair and top slab: z-1 stair y10 (the street eave, exactly at the clearance line), z0 slab, z1 stair y11, z2 slab, z3 stair y12, z4 slab, z5 ridge. The back slope mirrors it down to a z11 stair at y10. Front stairs face south and back stairs face north, so each slope descends toward its own face. A dark_oak verge on both gable edges and a dark_oak ridge give a crisp outline where the old roof dissolved into the walls. FIXED 2 (dormer was a shapeless lump): it is now a proper small dormer, front face at z1 x5-7. It has log cheeks, one glass pane at y11, plank cheeks z2-4, and a pitched cap at y13 (stairs east/west with a dark_oak slab spine). The cap overhangs to z0 as a little hood and runs into the main ridge. FIXED 3 (flat facade): the y6 row under every window is now a continuous course of upside-down spruce stairs, facing south toward the inside. The street sees only their upper half, so a shadow lip runs across the front without leaving the z0 plane. Every street-facing cell from y5 to y9 is still a solid block or pane. Side and back sills use the same trick, facing inward. FIXED 4 (sides read unfinished): both side walls have the full frame (posts z0/4/8/11, sole beam y5, plate y9), centred windows at z2 and z6 with sills, and a stripped-spruce mid-rail in the third bay for half-timber rhythm. The gables are finished too: a stripped-spruce tie beam at y10, plank infill, a pane vent at z5 y11, and a king-post stub at y12. FIXED 5 (back): it carries the same frame with three windows. The free back corners under the upper floor are now a covered yard: a store on the left with posts, barrels, a composter, a potted azalea and a hanging lantern; on the right, a stair climbing to the upper floor, with an azalea and a lantern. A brick chimney at x2 z8 rises through the back slope to a lit campfire at y13, so someone is home. CONTRACT: nothing outside x0-11 / z0-11 except the roof eave at z-1, which is at y10. Nothing at y1-4 in the stall fronts, R cells, H cells or stall walls/backs. All ground decor sits only in the free cells x0-3 and x9-11 at z9-11. Palette hierarchy: oak plank infill dominant; dark oak and stripped spruce frame; spruce roof with dark oak edges; lamps, glass and green as accents."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:oak_planks","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:dark_oak_log","minecraft:stripped_spruce_log","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:spruce_slab","minecraft:dark_oak_stairs","minecraft:dark_oak_slab","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:redstone_lamp","minecraft:bricks","minecraft:campfire","minecraft:barrel","minecraft:composter","minecraft:potted_flowering_azalea_bush","minecraft:flowering_azalea","minecraft:lantern"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[1,5,1],"to":[10,5,10],"block":"minecraft:spruce_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,6,0],"to":[11,8,0],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,6,11],"to":[11,8,11],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,6,0],"to":[0,8,11],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[11,6,0],"to":[11,8,11],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"line","from":[0,5,0],"to":[11,5,0],"block":"minecraft:stripped_spruce_log","state":{"axis":"x"}},{"op":"line","from":[0,9,0],"to":[11,9,0],"block":"minecraft